<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zipporah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zipporah appears in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-exodus">Book of Exodus</a> as the wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moses">Moses</a> and a daughter of Jethro, the priest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/midian">Midian</a>. According to Exodus, Moses defended Jethro's daughters at a well in Midian, and Jethro gave her to him. She bore two sons, Gershom and Eliezer. In an obscure passage at an inn on the road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, she circumcises her son and God spares Moses; the details are debated. Later, Jethro brings her and her sons to Moses in the wilderness of Sinai. Numbers 12 mentions a Cushite wife of Moses, and interpreters differ on whether this is Zipporah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zipporah.jpg" alt="Zipporah" width="330" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Ruskin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zipporah_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
